cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "OpenCashFlow: Cash-flow underwriting for SME credit risk"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-21
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/opencashflow/opencashflow"
url: "https://github.com/opencashflow/opencashflow"
abstract: >-
  An open-source cash-flow underwriting toolkit for B2B and SME credit risk. It turns
  open-banking-style transactions into 151 documented cash-flow features, probability-of-default
  scores and explainable decisions, with LimiX-2 as the primary tabular foundation model and
  LightGBM, XGBoost, logistic regression and a heuristic scorecard as baselines.
keywords:
  - credit risk
  - cash flow
  - SME
  - open banking
  - probability of default
  - tabular foundation model
  - LimiX
authors:
  - name: "OpenCashFlow contributors"
    affiliation: "Open source community"
